issues.suggested_fix:
Make the declaration and definition consistent. The simplest fix is to update the template header to declare save(const std::string &i_filename) instead of write(...), since the implementation and main() call use save. Concretely, in example_program/src/Bitmap24.hpp change the method prototype

    void write(const std::string &i_filename);

to

    void save(const std::string &i_filename);

(or alternatively rename the implementation to Bitmap24::write and update calls in main.cpp). Ensure the template repository's header, implementation, and example usage all use the same method name/signature so students can compile and run the example without linker errors.
